Why This Market Matters
Germanium substrates serve specialized applications where material properties, crystal quality, lattice compatibility, and infrared performance are critical. The market remains technically concentrated because suppliers must meet demanding requirements involving dislocation control, wafer thickness, orientation, doping, surface roughness, and epi-ready cleanliness. Recycling and reusable-substrate technologies are also becoming increasingly relevant as manufacturers seek to improve material economics and supply resilience.

